          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Story of Numbers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "shall take a glimpse of some of them. We will not be looking at different systems in a chronological order, but rather an order that shows us the main stages in the development of the idea of number representation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.144,
            0.848,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But first, let us explore some of the foundational ideas needed to count and to determine the number of objects in a given collection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.197,
            0.492,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Mechanism of Counting"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.228,
            0.847,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Imagine that we are living in the Stone Age, say, around ten thousand years ago. Suppose we have a herd of cows. Here are some natural questions that we might ask about our herd—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.295,
            0.77,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Q1. How do we ensure that all cows have returned safely after grazing?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.35,
            0.628,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q2. Do we have fewer cows than our neighbour?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.805,
            0.298,
            0.903,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.805,
                0.298,
                0.903,
                0.399
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.386,
            0.77,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Q3. If there are fewer, how many more cows would we need so that we have the same number of cows as our neighbour?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.429,
            0.77,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We need to tackle these questions without the use of the number names or written numbers of the Hindu number system. How do we do it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.485,
            0.502,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here are some possible methods."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.502,
            0.848,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We could tackle the questions by using pebbles, sticks or any object that is available in abundance. Let us choose sticks. For every cow in the herd, we could keep a stick. The final collection of sticks tells us the number of cows, which can be used to check if any cows have gone missing."
            }
          ]
        },
